    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0363" n="297" xml:id="pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00/3204: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-02T19:00:00-04:00">July 2, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. Your 71, July 2, 1 p.m. The President has decided to accede to the request of
                    the President of Haiti that complete withdrawal be effected by August 15th, but
                    he does not desire that this decision be made public until subsequent to his
                    conference with President Vincent on July 5th.</p>
                <p>The Navy Department has been confidentially informed and has advised this
                    Department that withdrawal can be completed by the date indicated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
